---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `Turn a number into Roman numerals. Up to 3999 is enough.
I want it as a procedure that hands the string back, so I
can use it in other programs.`;

const SampleOutput = `1990 -> MCMXC
2024 -> MMXXIV
4 -> IV`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-set-5" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 5
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Roman Numerals</h1>

        <p>
          <span class="badge text-bg-warning">Extra Credit</span>
          <span class="ms-2 text-body-secondary">Not part of the five required for this set.</span>
        </p>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code code={Brief} frame="code" lang="txt" title="What they asked for" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> Input,
            calculate, output, and anything you had to decide for yourself. See{" "}
            <a href="/courses/ap-csp/unit-2/cc-set-5">Set 5</a> for what that looks like.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Work out the algorithm on paper before writing anything. This one punishes coding first.</li>
            <li>The subtractive cases &mdash; IV, IX, XL, XC, CD, CM &mdash; are where every attempt breaks.</li>
            <li>Test 4, 9, 14, 40, 90, 400, 1990, and 3999. If all eight work, it works.</li>
            <li>There is a way to do this with a list and a loop that is far shorter than a wall of conditionals.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="sample-output">
          <h2>Sample Output</h2>

          <Code code={SampleOutput} frame="terminal" title="Sample Output" lang="txt" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />

          <p class="mt-3">MCMXC is the one that catches people. Check it character by character.</p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program file, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-roman-numerals</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
